{"unit":9,"items":54,"pass":38,"title":"Unit Test · Unit 9","tracks":{"a93":"Track_9.3.mp3"},"SEGS":{"both":["a93",3.82,128.16]},"html":"\n  <section class=\"stage on\" data-stage=\"Unit Test\">\n    <div class=\"stage-head\">\n      <div class=\"kicker\">Unit 9 &middot; Unit Test</div>\n      <h2>Looks and impressions</h2>\n      <p>Six parts, <b>54 questions</b>, covering everything in Unit 9, with four questions that come back from Units 1&ndash;8. Answer them all, then press Check. You need <b>38 out of 54</b> to pass. Parts 7 and 8 are your writing and speaking &mdash; they are not marked automatically, but do not skip them. You can take this test as many times as you like.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"task\" data-task data-tid=\"review-u9\">\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 1 · VOCABULARY ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\">Part 1 &middot; Vocabulary &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 1&ndash;12</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the word that fits.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">1</span><span class=\"body\">His hair falls just past his ears &mdash; it is&hellip;\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">spiky</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">shoulder-length</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">clean-shaven</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">2</span><span class=\"body\">He shaves every morning, so he is always&hellip;\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">well-built</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">bald</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">clean-shaven</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">3</span><span class=\"body\">The shape in the corner is not a person or an object &mdash; just a coloured&hellip;\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">blob</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">curtain</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">sketch</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">4</span><span class=\"body\">The delivery arrived damaged and nobody answered my email. I was extremely&hellip;\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">detailed</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">irritated</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">historic</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Match the two halves of each phrase. Click one on the left, then one on the right.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">5&ndash;9</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"pairbox\">\n          <div class=\"pcol\">\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"j1\">come</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"j2\">make</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"j3\">side</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"j4\">look</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"j5\">go</button>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"pcol\">\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"j4\" data-short=\"forward to\">forward to</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"j1\" data-short=\"up with a plan\">up with a plan</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"j5\" data-short=\"bald\">bald</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"j3\" data-short=\"by side\">by side</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"j2\" data-short=\"out the far side\">out the far side</button>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete each sentence with one word from the box: <b>foreground &middot; reflection &middot; description</b>.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">10</span><span class=\"body\">The two women are in the <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"foreground\" data-why=\"The <b>foreground</b> is the part nearest the viewer.\"> , and the river is behind them.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">11</span><span class=\"body\">That is not a window &mdash; it is a <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"reflection\" data-why=\"A <b>reflection</b> in a mirror.\"> in a mirror.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">12</span><span class=\"body\">The artist drew the face from a stranger&rsquo;s <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"description\" data-why=\"A <b>description</b> = the words somebody uses to describe something.\"> .</span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 2 · GRAMMAR ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 2 &middot; Grammar &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 13&ndash;26</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the correct form.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">13</span><span class=\"body\">Her hair is&hellip; curlier than it was last year.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">by far</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">more</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">much</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">14</span><span class=\"body\">That is&hellip; the most detailed sketch in the room.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">by far</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">much</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">slightly</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">15</span><span class=\"body\">He is not&hellip; as well-built as his brother.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">far</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">nearly</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">much</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">16</span><span class=\"body\">Of the two sisters, she is definitely&hellip;\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">the tallest</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">more tall</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">the taller</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the modal that fits the evidence.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">17</span><span class=\"body\">People are skating on it, so the river&hellip; frozen.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">might be</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">must be</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">can&rsquo;t be</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">18</span><span class=\"body\">Look at the clothes. It&hellip; a modern painting.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">must be</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">might be</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">can&rsquo;t be</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">19</span><span class=\"body\">Those blobs&hellip; birds, or they could be smoke.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">might be</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">must be</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">can&rsquo;t be</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Now or earlier? Choose.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">20</span><span class=\"body\">She must have been exhausted. <select data-answer=\"E\" data-why=\"<b>about an earlier moment</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"N\">about now</option><option value=\"E\">about an earlier moment</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">21</span><span class=\"body\">It can&rsquo;t be his. <select data-answer=\"N\" data-why=\"<b>about now</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"N\">about now</option><option value=\"E\">about an earlier moment</option></select></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete each sentence with the correct form.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">22</span><span class=\"body\">She is <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"taller\" data-why=\"A comparative never takes <b>more</b> and <i>-er</i> together: <i>taller</i>.\"> than her brother.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">23</span><span class=\"body\">It simply <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"can’t be|cannot be\" data-why=\"The confident negative deduction is <b>can&rsquo;t be</b>, never <i>mustn&rsquo;t be</i>.\"> a photograph.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">24</span><span class=\"body\">That is certainly <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"the most old-fashioned\" data-why=\"A superlative always takes <b>the</b>: <i>the most old-fashioned</i>.\"> picture here.</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Write the second sentence so that it means the same as the first.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">25</span><span class=\"body\">This sketch is far more detailed than that one.<br>That sketch is <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"nothing like as detailed as this one|not nearly as detailed as this one\" data-why=\"Reverse the comparison and keep the size of the gap.\"></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">26</span><span class=\"body\">I am certain somebody moved it during the night.<br>Somebody <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"must have moved it during the night|must have moved it\" data-why=\"A deduction about the past &rarr; <b>must have</b> + past participle.\"></span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 3 · READING ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 3 &middot; Reading &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 27&ndash;34</span></div>\n      <p class=\"subline\">Read the whole text once before you answer anything.</p>\n\n      <article class=\"reading\">\n        <h3>The face in the photograph</h3>\n        <p class=\"stand\">Passport officers, border staff and jurors are all asked to decide whether two photographs show the same person. Almost nobody is any good at it.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">A</span>In a study at an Australian university, passport officers were shown pairs of photographs and asked a single question: same person, or different? They were wrong about one time in seven. That is roughly the rate produced by students who had never done the job and had five minutes of instruction. Experience, it turned out, made almost no difference at all.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">B</span>The reason is that we are extremely good at recognising faces we know and surprisingly bad at matching faces we do not. A familiar face is stored as something like a summary, built from hundreds of sightings in different light and at different angles. An unfamiliar face is only ever the photograph in front of you, and a change of lighting can alter it more than a change of person does.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">C</span>This has a practical consequence that courts have been slow to accept. A witness who says &ldquo;that is definitely the man&rdquo; may be reporting a real feeling of certainty; the feeling simply is not evidence. Researchers have shown that confidence and accuracy are only loosely connected in unfamiliar face matching, and that the people who are most certain are not reliably the people who are most often right.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">D</span>There is one group that does much better. A small number of people, sometimes called super-recognisers, match unfamiliar faces far more accurately than everybody else, and several police forces now test for them and employ them deliberately. Nobody yet knows what they are doing differently, and they cannot explain it themselves. They just look, and they are right.</p>\n      </article>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the best answer.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">27</span><span class=\"body\">What did the Australian study find about experience?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">it made officers much more accurate</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">it made officers slower</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">it made almost no difference to accuracy</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">28</span><span class=\"body\">According to paragraph B, why is an unfamiliar face harder?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">you have only the one image, so lighting can change it more than identity does</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">people photograph badly when they are nervous</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">the photographs are usually too small</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">True, False, or Not given? Choose for each sentence.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">29</span><span class=\"body\">The officers were wrong about one time in seven. <select data-answer=\"T\" data-why=\"Paragraph A says exactly that.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option><option value=\"T\">True</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">30</span><span class=\"body\">Confident witnesses are reliably the most accurate. <select data-answer=\"F\" data-why=\"Paragraph C: confidence and accuracy are only <b>False</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"T\">True</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">31</span><span class=\"body\">Super-recognisers are born with the ability. <select data-answer=\"N\" data-why=\"The text says nobody knows what they do differently; where it comes from is never discussed.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">32</span><span class=\"body\">Some police forces test for super-recognisers. <select data-answer=\"T\" data-why=\"Paragraph D says several forces test for them and employ them.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option></select></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Answer the last two questions about the whole text.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">33</span><span class=\"body\">In paragraph C, &ldquo;the feeling simply is not evidence&rdquo; means that\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">witnesses usually lie about being sure</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">being certain does not make an identification correct</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">courts should never hear witnesses at all</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">34</span><span class=\"body\">The last two sentences of the text suggest that super-recognisers\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">are accurate without being able to say why</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">have been fully explained by researchers</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">are wrong as often as everybody else</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 4 · LISTENING ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 4 &middot; Listening &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 35&ndash;40</span></div>\n      <p class=\"subline\">Read the questions first. Then play the recording twice.</p>\n\n      <div class=\"player\">\n        <button class=\"btn btn-audio\" onclick=\"playClip('both',this,'Stop')\">\n          <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg> Two people, two paintings\n        </button>\n        <div class=\"wave\"></div>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><b>Navigate B1+ &middot; Audio 9.3</b>Original coursebook recording</div>\n      </div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete the notes with one word.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">35</span><span class=\"body\">In the bottom left corner of the first painting there are some men with <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"dogs\" data-why=\"Men with <b>dogs</b> in the bottom left-hand corner.\"> .</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">36</span><span class=\"body\">The speaker decides that the curved shape behind the woman is a <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"mirror\" data-why=\"She decides it is a <b>mirror</b>.\"> .</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">37</span><span class=\"body\">What is reflected in it: the sea and two old-fashioned sailing <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"ships\" data-why=\"Two old-fashioned sailing <b>ships</b>.\"> .</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the best answer.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">38</span><span class=\"body\">She says &ldquo;It must be either an old painting or a painting of a historical scene.&rdquo; She says this because of\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">the frame</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">the artist&rsquo;s name</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">the clothes and the way of life she can see</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">39</span><span class=\"body\">&ldquo;I&rsquo;m not sure exactly what they&rsquo;re doing!&rdquo; This tells you she is\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">honest about the limits of what she can see</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">pretending not to know</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">bored by the painting</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">40</span><span class=\"body\">What is the speaker doing throughout both descriptions?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">reading an official description aloud</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">reasoning out loud from what she can see</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">comparing the two paintings with each other</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 5 · FUNCTIONAL LANGUAGE ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 5 &middot; Functional language &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 41&ndash;48</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">What would you say? Choose the phrase that fits.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">41</span><span class=\"body\">You are opening a complaint in person, and you want to stay reasonable.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">Right, listen.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">I&rsquo;m sorry to have to say this, but&hellip;</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">That&rsquo;s a fair point.</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">42</span><span class=\"body\">You are asking for the problem to be put right, as softly as possible.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">Sort it out now.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">This is unacceptable.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">Is there any chance of a replacement?</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">43</span><span class=\"body\">You are disagreeing online, and you want the other person to keep reading.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">I see your point about the noise, but I&rsquo;d have to disagree with the conclusion.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">Anybody who thinks this is fine has not been reading.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">That is simply nonsense.</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Would each line work in a public post, or would it lose the reader?</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">44&ndash;47</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"sortbox\">\n          <div class=\"sortpool\"><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Works\">That&rsquo;s a fair point about the noise.</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Loses\">Anybody who thinks this is fine has not been reading.</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Works\">In my view the problem isn&rsquo;t the closure &mdash; it&rsquo;s that nobody asked.</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Loses\">You clearly have no idea what you are talking about.</button></div>\n          <div class=\"sortcols\"><div class=\"sortcol\" data-col=\"Works\"><h5>It belongs here</h5><div class=\"drop\"></div></div><div class=\"sortcol\" data-col=\"Loses\"><h5>It would lose the reader</h5><div class=\"drop\"></div></div></div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Put the four parts of the post in order.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">48</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"order\" data-order=\"d3,d1,d4,d2\">\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"d1\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">The path has been closed since April, and about thirty of us use it every Saturday.</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"d2\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">I&rsquo;d suggest two things. First, share our counts. Second, ask before closing, not after.</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"d3\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">I see your point about the nesting season, but I&rsquo;d have to disagree with the conclusion.</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"d4\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">In my view the problem isn&rsquo;t the closure &mdash; it&rsquo;s that nobody asked.</span></button>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 6 · PUTTING IT TOGETHER ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 6 &middot; Putting it together &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 49&ndash;54</span></div>\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete the conversation. Two of these gaps come back from earlier units. <span class=\"pill-rec\">recycled</span></p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"chat\">\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Madina</b>Have you seen the two sketches side by side?</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>Yes. The self-described one is <select data-answer=\"far sadder\" data-why=\"A big gap &rarr; <b>far sadder</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>more sadder</option><option>far sadder</option><option>by far sadder</option></select> than the stranger&rsquo;s.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Madina</b>And older, I thought.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>Only <select data-answer=\"slightly\" data-why=\"A tiny gap &rarr; <b>slightly</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>by far</option><option>much the</option><option>slightly</option></select> older. But it is <select data-answer=\"nothing like as\" data-why=\"<b>nothing like as</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>nothing like as</option><option>far as</option><option>not so much</option></select> detailed around the eyes.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Madina</b>Do you think he had a photograph?</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>He <select data-answer=\"can&rsquo;t have had\" data-why=\"A confident negative about the past &rarr; <b>can&rsquo;t have had</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>mustn&rsquo;t have had</option><option>can&rsquo;t have had</option><option>might not have</option></select> one &mdash; he was behind a curtain.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Madina</b>The company paid for the whole thing, you know.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b><span class=\"pill-rec\">recycled</span> <select data-answer=\"That&rsquo;s a fair point,\" data-why=\"Concedes before disagreeing. <b>That&rsquo;s a fair point,</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>You&rsquo;re completely wrong,</option><option>That&rsquo;s a fair point,</option><option>I couldn&rsquo;t agree more,</option></select> but it does not explain why the film worked. If nobody <select data-answer=\"had recognised\" data-why=\"An unreal past condition &rarr; past perfect. <b>had recognised</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>had recognised</option><option>recognised</option><option>would recognise</option></select> the gap, it would have gone nowhere.</div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <button class=\"btn btn-primary\" onclick=\"checkReview(this)\" style=\"margin-top:24px\">Check my answers</button>\n      <div class=\"res\"></div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div id=\"reviewResult\" class=\"review-result\"></div>\n\n    <!-- ============ PART 7 · WRITING ============ -->\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:30px\">Part 7 &middot; Writing &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">assessed against the criteria</span></div>\n    <p class=\"subline\">Write 120&ndash;140 words. Give yourself twenty-five minutes.</p>\n    <div class=\"opentask\" data-open data-tid=\"test-write\">\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"body\">\n        <p class=\"ohint\"><b>The task.</b> Somebody in an online group has argued that a local decision &mdash; a closure, a rule, a price rise &mdash; was the right one. Write a reply disagreeing. Agree with two things first. State your disagreement once. Give evidence with dates or numbers. Say what the real problem is, in your view. Finish with two specific suggestions and a question to somebody else in the group.</p>\n        <textarea placeholder=\"I see your point about&hellip;, and that&rsquo;s a fair point about&hellip;   But I&rsquo;d have to disagree with&hellip;   It has been&hellip; since&hellip;   In my view the problem isn&rsquo;t&hellip;   I&rsquo;d suggest two things&hellip;\" data-track></textarea>\n      </span></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"bubble useful\">\n      <div class=\"blab\">Your post must contain</div>\n      <ul>\n        <li>two things you agree with, <b>before</b> the disagreement</li>\n        <li>the disagreement stated once, not repeated</li>\n        <li>at least two numbers or dates as evidence</li>\n        <li>one deduction: <b>There must be a reason they&hellip;</b></li>\n        <li>one comparison: <b>considerably further than&hellip; / nothing like as&hellip; as&hellip;</b></li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- ============ PART 8 · SPEAKING ============ -->\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 8 &middot; Speaking &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">assessed against the criteria</span></div>\n    <div class=\"opentask speak\" data-open data-tid=\"test-speak\">\n      <div class=\"sp-head\"><span class=\"sp-ic\">&#127908;</span>\n        <div><b>Speaking &mdash; describe, deduce, complain</b><span>Extended turn</span></div></div>\n      <p class=\"sp-task\"><b>Part A.</b> Think of a photograph or painting you know. Describe it and speculate about it for a minute: what must be true, what might be true, what cannot be true, and what must have happened just before it. <b>Part B.</b> Then complain, out loud, about something that has genuinely annoyed you &mdash; open it, say what is wrong, and ask for the fix.</p>\n      <ul class=\"sp-list\">\n        <li>three degrees of certainty: <b>must be / might be / can&rsquo;t be</b></li>\n        <li>one deduction about an earlier moment, with <b>have</b> in it</li>\n        <li>two comparisons with different modifiers</li>\n        <li>a complaint that never accuses the person in front of you</li>\n      </ul>\n      <div class=\"sp-lang\"><b>Use this language</b>It must be&hellip; &middot; It might well be&hellip; &middot; It can&rsquo;t be&hellip; &middot; Somebody must have&hellip; &middot; far more&hellip; than &middot; nothing like as&hellip; as &middot; I&rsquo;m sorry to have to say this, but&hellip; &middot; Would you mind&hellip;ing?</div>\n      <div class=\"rec\">\n        <div class=\"rec-row\">\n          <button class=\"rec-btn\" type=\"button\" onclick=\"recToggle(this)\" aria-label=\"Record your answer\" title=\"Record\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M12 14a3 3 0 0 0 3-3V6a3 3 0 0 0-6 0v5a3 3 0 0 0 3 3zm5-3a5 5 0 0 1-10 0H5a7 7 0 0 0 6 6.9V21h2v-3.1A7 7 0 0 0 19 11z\"/></svg></button>\n          <div class=\"rec-label\"><b>Record your answer</b><span>Press the microphone and speak</span></div>\n          <div class=\"rec-wave\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>\n          <div class=\"rec-time\">0:00</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"rec-takes\"></div>\n        <div class=\"rec-note\">Record it, play it back, then submit it for assessment.</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:30px\">Parts 7 and 8 &middot; Assessment</div>\n    <p class=\"subline\">These two parts are not marked automatically and they are not marked by you. Submit your writing and record your speaking, then your teacher &mdash; or the AI tutor &mdash; scores each part against the criteria below and writes the feedback.</p>\n    <div class=\"rubric-slot\">\n      <ul class=\"reqlist\">\n        <li>I agreed with two things before I disagreed with anything</li>\n        <li>I stated my disagreement once and then moved on</li>\n        <li>my post contains real numbers or dates, not only opinions</li>\n        <li>my suggestions are specific enough to act on</li>\n        <li>I used three different degrees of certainty when I spoke</li>\n        <li>every deduction about the past had <i>have</i> in it</li>\n        <li>my modifiers matched the size of the gap I meant</li>\n        <li>my complaint never blamed the person I was speaking to</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n"}